  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tanzania delegation to Startup Conference DR Congo, Kinshasa</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Netherlands Embassy in Tanzania is supporting the Tanzania Start-up Association (TSA) in establishing and implementing a Tanzanian Start-up act. To kickstart the next phase of this process the Embassy proposes to send TSA, together with relevant government officials to the Start-up Conference in Kinshasa. With this, the project partners hope to:-	Inspire Tanzania through multilateral discussions;-	Form regional ties and stimulate regional knowledge exchange;-	Offer TSA and Tanzanian government knowledge of the Democratic Republic of the Congo (DRC) ecosystem.About the conference in the Democratic Republic of the Congo (DRC)The goal of the conference on implementing the Start-up Act in DRC is to raise awareness and inform entrepreneurs and stakeholders about this recently adopted law and the changes it will bring.Also, the conference should facilitate the dialogue between stakeholders and the government authorities responsible for implementation on the next steps to be taken. Although the outcome of this dialogue is of course still unknown, expectations are that at least part of the recommended measures will be adopted.</narrative>
  </description>
